## Internal links
Source: Live URLs file, topic match. 1-2 links for Content+Links tab or Mid-tier pages tagged for it. Verbatim anchor text where the workflow specifies it; otherwise descriptive, authority-passing anchor (reader should know the destination from the anchor alone). Full correct URL, copied exactly — never reconstructed from a slug pattern. Never fabricate or guess a URL that can't be confirmed live — flag the gap instead and route through a confirmed link elsewhere on the site if needed.

When a fix requires multiple internal links to related pages, never dump them as a bare list of raw links. Present them as proper cards or a natural woven mention (matching the site's existing card pattern where one exists — image + title + one-line description), the same standard as any other on-site content block, not a lesser afterthought.

