## Output format — every single time

Output is **edits to make directly in the shared `.md` file** — not a description of changes. For each piece:
- New title tag → exact new line
- New meta description → exact new line
- New section copy (only if B-bucket) → exact markdown to insert, with where it goes (after which heading)
- Content trim/edit (only if C2-bucket) → exact old text → exact new text (or "delete this passage")
- Internal link(s): source page → anchor text → exact line/sentence it's woven into (only when applicable)
- Query classification notes: one line per meaningfully-sized query that's B, C1, or C2 — query name + bucket + one-line reason
- One line max on the overall why (e.g. "query X has 4.2k impressions, C2 tangent, trimmed")

**No walls of text. No recaps. No explaining the process back. Just the exact edits, ready to paste into the .md file.** If something's genuinely ambiguous, ask one short question — don't guess silently, don't over-explain the guess.

